{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ובמדבר אשר ראית", :translit "u-va-midbar asher ra'ita", :gloss "and in the wilderness where you saw"} {:he "כל הדרך אשר הלכתם", :translit "kol ha-derech asher halachtem", :gloss "all the way that you walked"} {:he "ל' יחיד", :translit "lamed yachid", :gloss "lamed singular"} {:he "ל' רבים", :translit "lamed rabim", :gloss "lamed plural"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Grammar: the same word כל in our verse carries a singular ל' in הלכתם, while other occurrences use the plural לכם."}], :frame {:text "The clouds of glory that accompanied Israel in the wilderness performed individualized miracles for each person. Targum Yonatan renders Numbers 10:34 to say the cloud wiped away snakes, scorpions, and thorns, leveling every high and low place. The Mekhilta on Exodus 13:21 records that the cloud flattened the wilderness terrain for Israel's travel.", :sources ["Targum Yonatan Num 10:34" "Mekhilta d'Rabbi Yishmael Bo 14 (Exod 13:21)"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Grammar: the same word כל in our verse carries a singular ל' in הלכתם, while other occurrences use the plural לכם.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:33:24.809076545Z", :model "glm-5.2"}